TEXT 56 376 Left 5 ;Leakage, ironlost and cu-lost \nnot considered (R=R1=18.9 R2=2.1 Rfe=8654 Rphis=1.178e7)
TEXT 56 -144 Left 2 ;Why not smaller B values for transformers\nBecause:\nIf B should be lowered Area has to be higher -> more iron \nIf B should be lowered N has to be higher -> more copper\nThe formula is:\nU=4.44*fN*N*B*area\nHINT: \nTry to set N higher\nTry to ser A higher\nSEE: If you set N higher and also A lower -> B=constant\nand Phi gets proportional smaller and imue gets quadratic smaller\nimue=length/(mue0*muer*area*N)*Phi\nIf N gets smaller Phi gets smaller and -> imue gets quadratic smaller\nIf A gets higher B gets smaller and imue gets proportional smaller\nPhi remains constant Phi=B.A=const
